
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">To what extent is the &#8220;the story about the analytic turn&#8221; in philosophy a story about politics?</p>



<span id="more-26587"></span>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">There&#8217;s been an increased discussion in recent years of <a href="https://dailynous.com/2023/12/01/externalist-explanations-of-philosophy/">externalist explanations</a> of philosophy, and one such explanation that has gotten a fair amount of attention lately is the idea that McCarthyist anti-communism in the United States in the middle of the 20th Century played a significant role in analytic philosophy&#8217;s emerging dominance in the discipline at the time. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In the following guest post, <a href="https://www.sanderverhaegh.nl/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Sander Verhaegh</a> of Tilburg University, shows how the picture is quite a bit more complicated than that, casting doubt on how much the &#8220;McCarthyist thesis&#8221; can explain. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The post grew out of research Professor Verhaegh conducted for his just-published book, <a href="https://global.oup.com/academic/product/logical-positivism-9780197537961?cc=us&amp;lang=en&amp;"><em>Logical Positivism: An American History</em></a> (also <a href="https://www.sanderverhaegh.nl/publications.html">here</a> and <a href="https://www.amazon.com/Logical-Positivism-American-Sander-Verhaegh/dp/0197537960?crid=294MPH6THGKED&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.kGKwt1OQKiJCoZZBsiBKmlc8xcYqM1oGyJ18sSUGYilPGPOxD1uv_cWnUreSiC0IPnQb3rWIJiw7IwUUZEjoAUE5P4BYzDnmHrIbgsdQKJYH7kswlQkZMQjf6l37TKYWniWToya12XJ0WA0-ASSh8AdczfcwdbRPgs4oB7L6EnJ9gYF4K0Le6h6HbFgqITvA-y2eP2zN6V3bGb0RxMxf77Bd6YroF4UXevxlQRqb8jY._xxRwJS_77q40k4IO0e-M-XUSR7ZgdO1WAy7GYzq8wU&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=Logical+Positivism%3A+An+American+History&amp;qid=1790652493&amp;sprefix=logical+positivism+an+american+history%2Caps%2C206&amp;sr=8-1&amp;linkCode=ll2&amp;tag=dainou-20&amp;linkId=da186c7e1d45f43d9f918300aeab35a2&amp;language=en_US&amp;gaOptInStatus=true&amp;ref_=as_li_ss_tl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">here</a>).</p>



